  "body": "## Vulnerability details\n\nHyperliquid's 0x811 precompile (PRECOMPILE_SUPPLIED_BALANCE) returns the full BorrowLendUserTokenState struct containing four uint64 fields: borrow.basis, borrow.value, supply.basis, supply.value. PrecompileReader.suppliedBalance() only extracts the fourth field (supply.value) when decoding, completely discarding the borrow information in the first two fields.\n\n```solidity\nfunction suppliedBalance(address account, uint64 token) internal view returns (uint64 supplied) {\n    (bool ok, bytes memory res) = HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_SUPPLIED_BALANCE.staticcall(\n        abi.encode(account, token)\n    );\n    require(ok && res.length >= 128, \"PrecompileReader: supplied balance read failed\");\n    (,,, supplied) = abi.decode(res, (uint64, uint64, uint64, uint64));\n}\n```\n\nMonetrixAccountant._readL1Backing() iterates over all registered SuppliedAssets, accumulating supply values into total via suppliedUsdcEvm() or suppliedNotionalUsdcFromPerp(), without ever subtracting borrow values at any point.\n\n```solidity\nuint256 slen = suppliedList.length;\nfor (uint256 i = 0; i < slen; i++) {\n    SuppliedAsset storage a = suppliedList[i];\n    if (a.spotToken == uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX)) {\n        total += int256(PrecompileReader.suppliedUsdcEvm(account));\n    } else {\n        total += int256(\n            PrecompileReader.suppliedNotionalUsdcFromPerp(uint32(a.spotToken), a.perpIndex, account)\n        );\n    }\n}\n```\n\nPM is a fully planned and implemented feature path in the protocol, not a hypothetical scenario. The contracts contain setPmEnabled(), notifyVaultSupply(), PM branches in _sendL1Bridge(), and the entire 0x811 read pipeline, all specifically written for PM mode. Governor enabling PM via setPmEnabled(true) is an expected governance operation. Once PM is enabled, the Vault automatically registers 0x811 supplied slots in the Accountant when executing hedges and BLP operations, through executeHedge() and supplyToBlp().\n\nAfter PM is enabled, auto-borrow requires no attacker to trigger. The Hyperliquid PM engine automatically manages the Vault's L1 account borrowing based on market conditions (funding rate changes, collateral value fluctuations, margin requirement adjustments). This is a core PM mechanism, not an edge case. The Vault contract only has sendSupply (op=0) and sendWithdrawSupply (op=1) operations, with no explicit borrow operation, suggesting the protocol developers may not have anticipated that PM would produce borrow liabilities, which explains why PrecompileReader completely ignores the borrow fields.\n\ntotalBackingSigned() is therefore permanently inflated: suppose the Vault supplies 500,000 USDC and 200,000 USDC is auto-borrowed, the net value should be 300,000 USDC, but the Accountant counts the full 500,000 USDC. surplus() and distributableSurplus() inherit this inflated value. When the Operator calls settle(proposedYield) as part of normal duties, Gate 3 checks proposedYield <= distributableSurplus(). Because distributableSurplus includes 200,000 USDC of phantom surplus, Gate 3 does not block this yield distribution that should not have passed. settle() then transfers real EVM USDC into YieldEscrow, and the Operator distributes it via distributeYield() to sUSDM holders, InsuranceFund, and Foundation. This constitutes direct loss of real funds, not merely functional impairment or availability issues.\n\nThis loss automatically repeats every settlement cycle without any human intervention. Gate 4's annualized APR cap (default 1200bps = 12%) only limits the extraction rate per settlement, it does not prevent cumulative losses. With 10M USDM supply, each 21-hour settlement cycle extracts approximately 6,904 USDC of phantom yield. Over 30 days across approximately 34 settlement cycles, this accumulates to roughly 234,000 USDC of real funds extracted. If the borrow persists or grows, the protocol will trend toward insolvency (backing < totalSupply) within months, violating the INV-1 solvency invariant. There is no on-chain alerting mechanism that can detect the inflated surplus, because totalBackingSigned() itself is the on-chain \"source of truth.\" Additionally, yieldShortfall() also uses the inflated surplus to determine how much yield to bridge from L1, further amplifying the fund outflow.\n\nThe attack path of this vulnerability does not depend on any hypothetical external conditions. PM enablement is a planned governance operation on the protocol roadmap, auto-borrow is an inherent PM mechanism, and the Operator calls settle() as part of normal duties. No step in the entire chain requires malicious behavior or unreasonable assumptions. Per the C4 High definition \"Assets can be stolen/lost/compromised directly (or indirectly if there is a valid attack path that does not have hand-wavy hypotheticals)\", the real USDC extracted from the protocol each settlement cycle constitutes direct fund loss, and no hand-wavy hypotheticals exist in the attack path.",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Concept\n\nThe following code is added to `test_submissionValidity` in `test/c4/C4Submission.t.sol`. A helper function `_mockVaultL1SuppliedUsdcWithBorrow` is added to set up 0x811 responses containing borrow fields (setUp is unmodified).\n\nThe PoC simulates a scenario where PM auto-borrow results in borrow = supply (net value = 0): the Vault supplies 500K USDC on L1 while the PM engine auto-borrows 500K USDC. The true L1 net value is zero, the true surplus is zero, but the Accountant reports 500K surplus. The Operator executes settle + distributeYield as part of normal duties, distributing pure phantom yield as real funds each cycle. After just 3 cycles (63 hours), the protocol becomes insolvent: USDM total supply exceeds true backing, and the INV-1 invariant is violated.\n\nFull `test_submissionValidity` function body and new helper function:\n\n```solidity\nfunction _mockVaultL1SuppliedUsdcWithBorrow(\n    uint64 borrowBasis,\n    uint64 borrowValue,\n    uint64 supplyBasis,\n    uint64 supplyValue\n) internal {\n    _PoCMockPrecompile(payable(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_SUPPLIED_BALANCE)).setResponse(\n        abi.encode(address(vault), uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX)),\n        abi.encode(borrowBasis, borrowValue, supplyBasis, supplyValue)\n    );\n}\n\nfunction test_submissionValidity() public {\n    // ============================================================\n    //  Setup: user1 deposits 1M USDC, stakes all into sUSDM\n    // ============================================================\n    _deposit(user1, 1_000_000e6);\n    _stake(user1, 1_000_000e6);\n\n    // Governor enables PM; vault registers a USDC supplied slot\n    vm.prank(admin);\n    vault.setPmEnabled(true);\n    vm.prank(address(vault));\n    accountant.notifyVaultSupply(uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX), 0);\n\n    // ============================================================\n    //  Simulate PM state: 500K supplied, 500K auto-borrowed\n    //  Net L1 asset = 0, but code reads gross 500K as backing\n    //  True surplus = (1M EVM + 0 L1 net) - 1M supply = 0\n    //  Reported surplus = (1M EVM + 500K gross) - 1M supply = 500K\n    // ============================================================\n    _mockVaultL1SuppliedUsdcWithBorrow(\n        500_000 * 1e8,  // borrow.basis (ignored by code)\n        500_000 * 1e8,  // borrow.value (ignored by code)\n        500_000 * 1e8,  // supply.basis\n        500_000 * 1e8   // supply.value (only this is read)\n    );\n\n    // Verify: true surplus is 0, but reported surplus is 500K\n    int256 reportedSurplus = accountant.surplus();\n    assertEq(reportedSurplus, 500_000e6, \"Reported surplus = 500K (should be 0)\");\n\n    // ============================================================\n    //  Snapshot BEFORE attack\n    // ============================================================\n    uint256 vaultUsdcBefore = usdc.balanceOf(address(vault));\n    uint256 usdmSupplyBefore = usdm.totalSupply();\n    uint256 foundationBefore = usdc.balanceOf(foundation);\n    uint256 insuranceBefore = usdc.balanceOf(address(insurance));\n\n    // ============================================================\n    //  Attack: 3 cycles of settle + distributeYield\n    //  Every USDC distributed is 100% phantom — true surplus is 0\n    // ============================================================\n    uint256 totalPhantomYield;\n    uint256 nextTime = 21 hours + 2;\n    for (uint256 cycle = 0; cycle < 3; cycle++) {\n        vm.warp(nextTime);\n\n        uint256 gate4Cap = (usdm.totalSupply() * 1200 * 21 hours) / (10_000 * 365 days);\n\n        vm.prank(operator);\n        vault.settle(gate4Cap);\n\n        vm.prank(operator);\n        vault.distributeYield();\n\n        totalPhantomYield += gate4Cap;\n        nextTime += 21 hours;\n    }\n\n    // ============================================================\n    //  End impact verification\n    // ============================================================\n    uint256 vaultUsdcAfter = usdc.balanceOf(address(vault));\n    uint256 foundationGain = usdc.balanceOf(foundation) - foundationBefore;\n    uint256 insuranceGain = usdc.balanceOf(address(insurance)) - insuranceBefore;\n    uint256 realUsdcExited = foundationGain + insuranceGain;\n    uint256 phantomUsdmMinted = usdm.totalSupply() - usdmSupplyBefore;\n\n    // 1) Real USDC permanently exited to Foundation (20%) and InsuranceFund (10%)\n    assertTrue(foundationGain > 0, \"Foundation received real USDC\");\n    assertTrue(insuranceGain > 0, \"InsuranceFund received real USDC\");\n\n    // 2) Unbacked USDM minted into sUSDM (70% of phantom yield)\n    assertTrue(phantomUsdmMinted > 0, \"USDM supply inflated without backing\");\n\n    // 3) INV-1 VIOLATED: true backing < USDM totalSupply\n    //    True backing = vault USDC (decreased) + L1 net (0)\n    //    USDM supply = original 1M + phantom minted (increased)\n    int256 trueBacking = int256(vaultUsdcAfter); // L1 net = 0\n    int256 usdmSupply = int256(usdm.totalSupply());\n    assertTrue(trueBacking < usdmSupply,\n        \"INSOLVENT: true backing < USDM supply (INV-1 violated)\");\n\n    // 4) Accounting identity: all phantom yield accounted for\n    assertEq(realUsdcExited + phantomUsdmMinted, totalPhantomYield,\n        \"Total damage = phantom yield settled\");\n\n    emit log_named_uint(\"Total phantom yield settled (USDC)\", totalPhantomYield);\n    emit log_named_uint(\"Real USDC exited to Foundation\", foundationGain);\n    emit log_named_uint(\"Real USDC exited to InsuranceFund\", insuranceGain);\n    emit log_named_uint(\"Phantom USDM minted into sUSDM\", phantomUsdmMinted);\n    emit log_named_uint(\"Vault USDC before\", vaultUsdcBefore);\n    emit log_named_uint(\"Vault USDC after\", vaultUsdcAfter);\n    emit log_named_int(\"True backing (vault USDC + 0 L1 net)\", trueBacking);\n    emit log_named_int(\"USDM total supply\", usdmSupply);\n    emit log_named_int(\"Insolvency gap (supply - backing)\", usdmSupply - trueBacking);\n}\n```\n\nDiff format (can be applied directly):\n\n```diff\n--- a/test/c4/C4Submission.t.sol\n+++ b/test/c4/C4Submission.t.sol\n@@ -315,10 +315,113 @@ contract C4Submission is Test {\n     //  at the end, with assertions proving the bug.\n     // ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n \n+    function _mockVaultL1SuppliedUsdcWithBorrow(\n+        uint64 borrowBasis,\n+        uint64 borrowValue,\n+        uint64 supplyBasis,\n+        uint64 supplyValue\n+    ) internal {\n+        _PoCMockPrecompile(payable(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_SUPPLIED_BALANCE)).setResponse(\n+            abi.encode(address(vault), uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX)),\n+            abi.encode(borrowBasis, borrowValue, supplyBasis, supplyValue)\n+        );\n+    }\n+\n     function test_submissionValidity() public {\n-        // ─── Placeholder — replace with your PoC ───\n-        // _deposit(user1, 10_000e6);\n-        // assertEq(usdm.balanceOf(user1), 10_000e6);\n-        // assertEq(usdc.balanceOf(address(vault)), 10_000e6);\n+        // ============================================================\n+        //  Setup: user1 deposits 1M USDC, stakes all into sUSDM\n+        // ============================================================\n+        _deposit(user1, 1_000_000e6);\n+        _stake(user1, 1_000_000e6);\n+\n+        // Governor enables PM; vault registers a USDC supplied slot\n+        vm.prank(admin);\n+        vault.setPmEnabled(true);\n+        vm.prank(address(vault));\n+        accountant.notifyVaultSupply(uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX), 0);\n+\n+        // ============================================================\n+        //  Simulate PM state: 500K supplied, 500K auto-borrowed\n+        //  Net L1 asset = 0, but code reads gross 500K as backing\n+        //  True surplus = (1M EVM + 0 L1 net) - 1M supply = 0\n+        //  Reported surplus = (1M EVM